# [CompliRules] HIPAA 45 CFR § 164.502(e) Business Associate Agreement (BAA) & Telemetry Guard
**Severity:** `CRITICAL` | **Jurisdiction:** `HIPAA_US`

<!-- NOTICE: CompliRules provides automated AST guardrails under CompliRules Free-to-Use License without warranty (See DISCLAIMER.md). Documentation: https://halilyilmz.github.io/complirules/ -->

## Legal Citations
- **HIPAA Privacy & Security Rules (45 CFR) (45 CFR § 164.502(e) & § 164.504(e))**: Disclosures to Business Associates: Covered entities may disclose PHI only to vendors with executed BAAs establishing permitted uses and strict security safeguards. *[Sanction: Tier 3/4 HIPAA civil monetary penalties up to $2,067,813 per violation category per year.]*
- **HHS OCR Resolution Agreements (Enforcement Precedents)**: OCR v. Raleigh Orthopaedic ($750k fine) and cloud enforcement cases penalizing un-sanitized exception dumps or PHI transmissions without BAAs.

## Rule Mandates
- MUST: MUST set sendDefaultPii: false in Sentry and crash reporting configurations.
- MUST: MUST implement beforeSend scrubbing filters redacting SSNs, MRNs (Medical Record Numbers), emails, and patient identifiers from error messages.
- MUST: NEVER initialize third-party LLM or telemetry APIs without verifying process.env.HIPAA_BAA_EXECUTED === "true" or an active enterprise BAA.
- MUST: MUST strip request cookies and authorization headers from outbound crash report payloads.

## Forbidden Anti-Patterns
- NEVER: Sentry.init with sendDefaultPii: true in healthcare applications
- NEVER: Streaming un-sanitized patient notes or raw exception traces to cloud telemetry without BAA

## Reference Compliant Code Snippets
### HIPAA-Compliant Sentry & PHI Scrubber
```typescript
import * as Sentry from '@sentry/nextjs';

const PHI_PATTERNS = {
  ssn: /\b\d{3}-\d{2}-\d{4}\b/g,
  mrn: /\bMRN[-:]?\s*\d{6,10}\b/gi,
  email: /\b[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Z|a-z]{2,}\b/g
};

export function initCompliantSentry() {
  Sentry.init({
    dsn: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN,
    sendDefaultPii: false,
    beforeSend(event) {
      if (event.exception?.values) {
        event.exception.values.forEach(exception => {
          if (exception.value) {
            exception.value = exception.value
              .replace(PHI_PATTERNS.ssn, '[REDACTED-SSN]')
              .replace(PHI_PATTERNS.mrn, '[REDACTED-MRN]')
              .replace(PHI_PATTERNS.email, '[REDACTED-EMAIL]');
          }
        });
      }
      if (event.request) {
        delete event.request.cookies;
        delete event.request.headers?.['authorization'];
        delete event.request.headers?.['cookie'];
      }
      return event;
    }
  });
}
```
